# Schema: Polkadot SDK PRDoc Schema (prdoc) v1.0.0
# See doc at https://raw.githubusercontent.com/paritytech/polkadot-sdk/master/prdoc/schema_user.json

title: Refactor `VerifySignature` transaction extension for signer compatibility

doc:
  - audience: Runtime Dev
    description: |
      Refactor the `pallet_verify_signature::VerifySignature` transaction extension from an enum
      with `Signed { .. }` / `Disabled` variants into a tuple struct
      `VerifySignature<T>(pub Option<VerifySignatureData<T>>)`, where `None` is the
      passthrough/disabled state and `Some(VerifySignatureData { signature, account })` carries
      the signature to verify.

      The motivation is signer compatibility. Generic signers can default extensions whose data
      is wrapped in an obvious "no-op" type such as `bool` or `Option<_>`, but cannot default an
      arbitrary enum without knowing its variants. Wrapping the extension data in an `Option`
      lets a signer that does not understand this extension simply encode `None` (a single
      `0x00` byte) to disable it.

      The public constructors `VerifySignature::new_with_signature(signature, account)` and
      `VerifySignature::new_disabled()` are preserved, so call sites that only use those
      constructors compile unchanged. Code that pattern-matched on the old `Signed { .. }` /
      `Disabled` variants directly must be updated to match on the wrapped `Option`.

      **On-chain encoding change.** This is a breaking change to the SCALE encoding of the
      extension. Under the old enum, `Disabled` encoded as variant tag `0x01` and `Signed` as
      `0x00`. With `Option<VerifySignatureData<T>>`, `None` encodes as `0x00` and `Some` as `0x01` —
      the tags for "disabled" and "signed" are flipped. To my knowledge, there is no production
      runtime using this extension right now, but this breaking change is reflected in the major
      bump of the pallet.

crates:
  - name: pallet-verify-signature
    bump: major
  - name: pallet-meta-tx
    bump: patch
  - name: pallet-example-authorization-tx-extension
    bump: patch
  - name: kitchensink-runtime
    bump: major
  - name: asset-hub-westend-runtime
    bump: major
  - name: collectives-westend-runtime
    bump: major
  - name: coretime-westend-runtime
    bump: major
  - name: people-westend-runtime
    bump: major
